1. **Lookahead IPv4 check** (`(?=.*\\b<IPv4>\\b)`): Verifies the line contains a valid IPv4 address\n2. **Greedy matching** (`.*`): Matches up to the last possible date (through regex backtracking within the line)\n3. **Date capture** with word boundaries: Validates YYYY-MM-DD with proper month/day rules\n   - 31-day months (01,03,05,07,08,10,12): days `0[1-9]|[12]\\d|3[01]`\n   - 30-day months (04,06,09,11): days `0[1-9]|[12]\\d|30`\n   - February: days `0[1-9]|[12]\\d|29`\n4. **Negative lookahead** (`(?!.*\\b<DATE>\\b)`): Ensures no more dates follow on this line\n\nThe regex ensures:\n- False matches like `1134-12-1234` or `192.168.1.11test` are rejected due to word boundaries\n- IPv4 octets without leading zeros (e.g., `192.168.1.1` but not `192.168.001.1`)\n- Only the last date per line is matched when multiple dates exist","ttft_ms":118132,"type":"result","duration_ms":128179,"uuid":"41a9906d-d0d0-40b1-a36e-c447a5030ef7","ttft_stream_ms":1081,"time_to_request_ms":81,"queued_turn_count":0}
